# Normalize line endings for the whole tree.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git decide per file whether content is text (and therefore
# eligible for normalization) or binary (left byte-for-byte untouched). `eol=lf`
# pins the checked-out and stored form of every text file to LF, so a checkout on
# Windows no longer introduces CRLF that a later `kairos-component-update` merge
# would surface as a whole-file line-ending diff. The tree was renormalized once
# when this file was added (`git add --renormalize .`); nothing else is needed.
#
# The component-update merge skill is intentionally unaware of these attributes —
# it LF-normalizes its own merge inputs — so this file exists purely to keep the
# committed template, and every component created from it, on LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
